#X text 30 380 The note inlet takes pitch - velocity - legato. Outlets: pitch (MIDI note \, 60 until the first note) - gate (0/1) - velocity (0..1). All three change at the very time the note comes: vline~ jumps there - where sig~ would wait for the next block. A note-on dips the gate for 1.5 ms so that it starts again \, unless it is legato: then only the pitch and velocity change.;
